crifices,-dispensing Dakshinas and kine by hundreds and thousands-and who has governed the earth by asceticism and truthful speech. His son Rāma has come to the forest through a woman.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-5-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4005006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd5f399e3a89b8638e2d725c4e81e10610a072c21e2e2f8e31cf381c9d7772c9","compact":"c7a0a7de045e87ba7c790c7412ce5363e9d28e2af4d088e5341c52f03267ccf5","nasal":"c7a0a7de045e87ba7c790c7412ce5363e9d28e2af4d088e5341c52f03267ccf5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-5-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":5,"verse":7,"english":"Do you, granting an interview to the brothers Rāma and Lakşmaņa-both of them worthy of homage-who pe eager for your friendship, receive them respectfully.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.339,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-5-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4005007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dc1348e2b99a9b08fae8a9ece73a60f9e83becd45ffc745842a502a2930c5264","compact":"2c114137bed4f270944202478bde5f45c29a64d7d78dee0cdaeb940ee88cd767","nasal":"2c114137bed4f270944202478bde5f45c29a64d7d78dee0cdaeb940ee88cd767"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-5-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":5,"verse":8,"english":"Hearing Hanuman's words, Sugrīva-lord of monkeys, becoming visible (at his will), gladly spoke to Rāghava, sir, you are versed in morality, and bear love towards all. The son of the wind-god has faithfully described your virtues to me.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.213,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-5-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4005008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"45e824e0